// Industries: the entry point of SafeWorks India and of every site in the SafeWorks Portal.
// One record per industry. The website shows an industry hub for each; the portal seeds a site's
// categories, checklists and library links from the same record.
//
// Schema
//   id        stable slug, also used by the portal (industry_profiles.code)
//   t         English name            n: {hi, ta, kn} names in the other UI languages
//   tag       one-line description shown on the tile
//   icon      key into ICONS in the shell (see the shell's ICONS map; new keys are added there)
//   est       establishment types the portal offers for a site in this industry:
//             factory | hazardous_process_factory | construction_site | mine | port | plantation | office | other
//   hazards   the 6–10 hazards that matter most, in order (shown first on the hub and used as search boosts)
//   tasks     3-step flow: common tasks/situations → each lists the library items that make up the "pack"
//             {id, t, procs:[proc ids], cks:[checklist ids], regs:[reg ids], talks:[talk titles], permits:[permit types]}
//   regs      regulation ids (REGS/REGS2/REGS4) that apply to the whole industry, most important first
//   procs     procedure ids (PROCS/PROCS2/PROCS3)
//   cks       checklist ids (CHECKLISTS/CHECKLISTS2/CHECKLISTS3/CHECKLISTS4)
//   talks     toolbox talk titles (TALKS/TALKS2/TALKS3/TALKS4)
//   ppe       mandatory PPE for the industry, shortest list first
//   statutory 4–8 one-line statutory duties specific to the industry (registration, officers, registers, returns)
//   cats      portal observation categories to pre-select for a new site (codes from the portal's category list)
//   kpis      1–3 industry KPIs worth watching beyond the common ones
//   sector    id of the matching SECTORS guide, when one exists (kept for the detailed TN/KA sector text)
//
// Only the fields marked "filled" below are complete in this file; the content pass fills the rest
// from the existing data files and adds the new procedures/checklists/talks (PROCS3, CHECKLISTS4, TALKS4).
